    "title": "'Virgin River' Season 8: Premiere Date Info, Cast Departures, And More",
    "text": "Published March 13, 2026, 12:30 p.m. ET Virgin River S7 - Trailer0 seconds of 1 minute, 57 secondsVolume 0% Where to Stream: Virgin River Where to Watch Widget Failed To Load. Please Try Again. Powered by Reelgood When the end credits roll on Virgin River Season 7, you’ll be screaming over one cliffhanger in particular — especially if you’re a Brady (Benjamin Hollingsworth) fan like me. Virgin River’s Season 7 finale finally saw Mel (Alexandra Breckenridge) and Jack (Martin Henderson) become parents, saw an unexpected new love triangle form in town, saw characters contemplating next steps, and finally showed Brie (Zibby Allen) and Brady happy. If only for a few moments! UGH! Does Brady survive Virgin River Season 7’s big cliffhanger? And what does the future hold for the rest of the small-town drama’s beloved characters? We need more episodes ASAP! Will there be a Virgin River Season 8? And if so, when will Virgin River return with new episodes? Here’s everything to know about the future of Virgin River, including Season 7 premiere date info, filming updates, cast departures, and comments from Virgin River stars Benjamin Hollingsworth and Zibby Allen. Virgin River Season 7 Ending Explained: Before we dive into Virgin River Season 8 news, you may need a refresher on Virgin River‘s Season 7 finale. If so, Decider’s got you covered! Read our Season 7 finale recap for an idea of what to expect from the show going forward, then read on to hear more about Virgin River‘s future. Will There Be A Virgin River Season 8 On Netflix? You bet! Netflix’s longest running drama is still going! The streamer officially renewed the hit drama for a Season 8 back in July 2025. And we’ve got good news on the production front… Photo: Courtesy of Netflix Virgin River Season 8 Filming Updates: Has Virgin River Season 8 Started Filming? During an interview with Decider, Virgin River‘s Ben Hollingsworth confirmed that production on Virgin River Season 8 is set to begin in April 2026. So stay tuned for more updates in the coming months! Virgin River Season 8 Premiere Date: When Does Virgin River Return With New Episodes On Netflix? As of Virgin River‘s Season 7’s premiere date (March 12, 2026), Netflix had yet to announce a Season 8 premiere date. But past premieres can offer some insight into when we could see new episodes. Season 1: December 6, 2019 Season 2: November 27, 2020 Season 3: July 9, 2021 Season 4: July 20, 2022 Season 5, Part 1: September 7, 2023 Season 5, Part 2: November 30, 2023 Season 6: December 19, 2024 Season 7: March 12, 2026 With the exception of Season 7, Netflix has released a new season of Virgin River every year since it premiered in 2019, so here’s hoping the series will return with Season 8 at some point in 2027. Stay tuned for more Season 8 updates and read on to learn Virgin River stars’ dream storylines! What Will Virgin River Season 8 Be About? Benjamin Hollingsworth And Zibby Allen Weigh In Virgin River Season 8 will continue to tell unfinished Season 7 finale stories and follow our favorite small-town characters. We’ll see Mel and Jack’s parenthood journey progress, learn how the Hope/Doc/Roland love triangle unfolds, and crucially learn Brady’s fate! “We don’t know if Brady survives. So if he’s back in Season 8, it’d be great to see him and Brie have some great sort of moment in their life that they could enjoy for a minute. I don’t even know that there’s a world in which Brady can have nice things. I always say he’s one of those people who just can’t have it. I don’t know if the audience is ever going to get that. So who knows? I mean, I know,” Hollingsworth told DECIDER over Zoom. Photo: Courtesy of Netflix If Brady does pull through, Hollingsworth and Allen have some Season 8 hopes. “I haven’t worked with a lot of the cast extensively, because Brady’s often to the side of the town. So people like Doc, who’s played by Tim Matheson, would be amazing to work with, and to have more scenes with the townspeople. Just to see him against a different energy would be really fun,” Hollingsworth said. The Virgin River star would also love to direct an episode one day! “I actually shadowed a director on Episode 9 and 10, because they do a block. Felipe Rodriguez, who’s a fantastic director. He directed the pool table scene and the motorcycle scene,” he said. “I would love to direct an episode at some point if they trust me enough to do so. I graduated from a pretty intense conservatory program after three years when I was like 19 to 21. So I really do have that training and understanding of the acting craft that allows me to communicate with actors.” As for Allen, she’s happy with what she’s heard of Brie’s Season 8 arc. “I think the writers have a great command over what these characters need and how to get them on their journey,” she said, noting her dreams for Brie. “[I’d like to ride] more horses! They’re going to be at my brother’s farm anyway. Let’s do this! That was such a cool experience,” she said. “And I’d love to see more Brie and Brady. There were times in the last two seasons where Ben and I were like, ‘I miss you!’Because our characters have had push and pull. So hopefully, depending on what happens with Brady’s accident, we’ll at least see them navigate a relationship in real terms for once.” Who’s Leaving Virgin River In Season 8? Two Longtime Cast Members Are Departing After Season 7 Two people fans won’t see in Virgin River Season 8 are Marco Grazzini, who plays Mike Valenzuela, and Lauren Hammersley, who’s played Charmaine since Season 1. While Char and Mike are leaving Virgin River, showrunner Patrick Sean Smith told Deadline that both characters could return in subsequent seasons, should the story allow. How Many Episodes Will Be In Virgin River Season 8? Like seasons past, Virgin River Season 8 will likely consist of 10 episodes. And if the past two seasons were any indication, we’ll likely get another full drop. Where To Watch Virgin River: Netflix Streaming Info Since Virgin River is a Netflix original, you’ll have to subscribe to the streamer to watch new and existing episodes. Here’s how! Netflix offers three subscription plans to fit your streaming needs. The plans start at $7.99/month for standard with ads and go up to $24.99/month for unlimited ad-free streaming in up to 4K UHD quality. Virgin River Season 7 is now streaming. Tags Benjamin Hollingsworth Netflix Virgin River",
